{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"e8671ebe-ecce-4916-b040-7c84c211bdfc","status":"SUCCESS","response":"### Target Files\n- `models.py`\n- `graph.py`\n- `scheduler.py`\n- `executor.py`\n\n### Symbols \u0026 Line Ranges\n- `models.py`: `Task.__post_init__` (lines 19–22)\n- `graph.py`: `Graph.topological_order` (lines 18–19)\n- `scheduler.py`: `Scheduler.should_skip` (lines 9–11)\n- `executor.py`: `Executor.run` (lines 11–25)\n\n### Invariants \u0026 Exact Changes\n- **`models.py` (`Task.__post_init__`, lines 19–22)**:\n  - Convert `self.dependencies = tuple(self.dependencies)` so it is always a defensive tuple copy (even if passed as a list or other iterable).\n  - Keep empty name check raising `ValueError(\"empty task name\")`.\n- **`graph.py` (`Graph.topological_order`, lines 18–19)**:\n  - Deduplicate dependency edges per task (e.g., `set(task.dependencies)`) when building adjacency/in-degree structures so duplicate dependency edges are treated as one edge.\n  - Implement Kahn's algorithm using `heapq` over ready nodes (in-degree 0) so that at every step the lexicographically smallest currently-ready node is selected.\n  - If `len(order) \u003c len(self.tasks)`, a cycle exists: find a concrete closed cycle path `[v, ..., v]` (first == last) following dependency edges (including self-loops `[a, a]`) among the remaining nodes, and raise `CycleError(cycle)`.\n  - Empty graph returns `[]`.\n- **`scheduler.py` (`Scheduler.should_skip`, lines 9–11)**:\n  - Return `True` if any direct dependency in `task.dependencies` has `status in (\"failed\", \"skipped\")` (currently only checks `\"failed\"`).\n- **`executor.py` (`Executor.run`, lines 11–25)**:\n  - Call `order = self.scheduler.plan()` before any handler invocation (ensuring cycles raise `CycleError` with no partial side effects).\n  - For each `name` in `order`: if `task.status in (\"succeeded\", \"failed\", \"skipped\")` (i.e. `task.status != \"pending\"`), skip execution/mutation so terminal tasks never execute again and their results/errors persist on reruns.\n  - Otherwise, if `self.scheduler.should_skip(task)`, set `task.status = \"skipped\"` and `task.error = \"upstream failure\"`.\n  - Otherwise invoke `self.handlers[name]()`, recording `task.result` and `task.status = \"succeeded\"`, or catching `Exception as exc` to set `task.status = \"failed\"` and `task.error = str(exc)`.\n  - Return `{name: self.graph.tasks[name].status for name in order}` (`{}` for empty graphs).\n\n### Verify Command\n`pytest -q --tb=short`\n","duration_seconds":6.9409881,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":27238,"output_tokens":1167,"thinking_tokens":88,"cache_read_tokens":22581,"total_tokens":28405}}}
